<title>Consolidated container Uganda → Hamburg · Run UG-GER-2026-09</title>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/images/favicon.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/zuricaf.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/landing.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <div class="cobrand">
    <a href="/"><img class="zuricaf" src="/images/zuricaf.png" alt="Zuricaf · Farmers Direct Sourcing Co." width="915" height="408"></a>
  </div>
  <div class="masthead">
    <span>Direct Trade Uganda</span>
    <span>Run UG-GER-2026-09 · Kampala → Hamburg</span>
  </div>

  <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:38px">Consolidated container · 20ft · 320 bags of 60 kg</p>
  <h1>19,200 kg fit into one container.<br>You need <em>600</em>.</h1>
  <p class="lead">We consolidate one container of Ugandan green coffee to Hamburg. You book your volume, we take care of export, freight, customs clearance and storage. What you pay depends on how full the container gets — so the whole calculation is open here.</p>

  <p class="note" style="margin-top:24px">Archive: example of a closed run. The terms of the next run may differ. Register interest: <a href="/next-run/">Next run</a>.</p>

  <p class="provisional">All rates provisional — final rate only after the freight costs are confirmed.</p>

  <div class="calc">
    <div class="calc-top">
      <span>One bar = one bag of 60 kg</span>
      <span id="bagcount">0 of 320 bags</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tally" id="tally" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="marks">
      <div class="mark" style="left:52.08%"><b></b><span>10 t · minimum volume</span></div>
      <div class="mark" style="left:78.13%"><b></b><span>15 t · rebate</span></div>
      <div class="mark" style="left:88.54%"><b></b><span>17 t</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="calc-in">
      <div class="field-lg">
        <label for="vol">Your volume in kg</label>
        <input type="number" id="vol" min="0" max="7000" step="60" value="1200" inputmode="numeric">
      </div>
      <div class="readout">
        <div class="ro" id="ro-rate"><b>Your rate</b><strong id="rate">–</strong><small id="tier">&nbsp;</small></div>
        <div class="ro"><b>Total logistics</b><strong id="total">–</strong><small>plus duty, import VAT, cess</small></div>
        <div class="ro"><b>Deposit 30%</b><strong id="dep">–</strong><small>due at booking</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section>
  <p class="sec-note">Why this exists</p>
  <div class="cols">
    <div>
      <h3>The container is the hurdle</h3>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:15px">You only get a lot of your own from Uganda if you fill a container. Most roasteries need 600 to 6,000 kg. In between there is nothing — except the importer who sells you his selection.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>You keep your supplier</h3>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:15px">You buy the coffee yourself, from the producer you want.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>One rate, no surprises</h3>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:15px">Everything from the collection point in Uganda to the warehouse in Hamburg is in one price per kilo. What is not in it is listed below — completely and item by item.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <p class="sec-note">Price scale</p>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:8px">The more you book, the less you pay per kilo.</h2>
  <p class="provisional" style="margin:0 0 20px">Provisional — final rate only after the freight costs are confirmed.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Volume</th><th class="r">Rate €/kg</th><th class="r">at 15 t fill</th><th class="r">at 17 t fill</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody id="ladder"></tbody>
  </table>
  <p style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:14px">
    If the container reaches 15,000 kg, every participant gets €0.08/kg back. From 17,000 kg it is €0.15/kg.
    Paid out after shipping. Above 7,000 kg we calculate individually.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <p class="sec-note">Scope of service</p>
  <div class="inout">
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px">Included in the rate</h3>
      <ul class="yes">
        <li>Receiving at our collection point in Uganda</li>
        <li>Bagging, screening, export marking</li>
        <li>Export clearance and documentation</li>
        <li>Road transport to Mombasa</li>
        <li>Sea freight to Hamburg</li>
        <li>Import clearance and terminal handling</li>
        <li>Unloading, sorting, free storage</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:12px">Not included, at cost</h3>
      <ul class="no">
        <li>The coffee itself — you buy it directly</li>
        <li>Cess: 2% on the declared export value</li>
        <li>Import duty and import VAT</li>
        <li>Transport insurance</li>
        <li>Storage beyond the free period</li>
        <li>Demurrage caused by missing papers or payment</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <p class="sec-note">Process</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><div><h3>Register your volume</h3><p>Form below. Within two working days you get a confirmation with your rate and the booking deadline.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>Book and pay the deposit</h3><p>30% deposit. This reserves your place. Until the booking deadline the rate is indicative, afterwards fixed.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>Your supplier delivers</h3><p>To our collection point in Uganda, uncleared and without export preparation. Big bags or GrainPro. You can send empty jute bags with your logo.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>We bag and ship</h3><p>Bagging, weighing, marking, export under one declaration for the whole container. The weighed net weight is the billing weight.</p></div></li>
    <li><div><h3>Pick-up in Hamburg</h3><p>After customs clearance and unloading you get the release notice. Your free storage starts from then.</p></div></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section>
  <p class="sec-note">Terms</p>
  <div class="terms">
    <p><b>Minimum volume per participant</b> 600 kg. Above that in steps of 60 kg, i.e. whole bags.</p>
    <p><b>The container sails from 10,000 kg</b> of total booked volume. If that is not reached, your deposit is refunded in full and you incur no costs.</p>
    <p><b>Rates are indicative until the booking deadline</b> and fixed afterwards — in both directions. The published scale is provisional until the freight costs are confirmed.</p>
    <p><b>Payment</b> 30% at booking, the rest before release in Hamburg.</p>
    <p><b>Billing weight</b> is the net weight weighed at bagging, not the registered volume.</p>
    <p><b>Rebate</b> from 15,000 kg €0.08/kg, from 17,000 kg €0.15/kg, the same for all participants.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="form">
  <p class="sec-note">Archive</p>
  <h2>Run UG-GER-2026-09</h2>
  <p class="lead">This page shows the run of September 2026 as an example. Registration goes through the <a href="/next-run/">next run</a>.</p>
</section>

